by Amoifr at 2026-04-29T09:25:53Z

Thanks @Kocal for kicking this off — really nice base, especially the anti-patterns table and the `<recipe>_<role>_attrs` formalization 🙌

I've been maintaining a similar skill on my side (FR, Shadcn-focused), built up incrementally from the review feedback I got across recent recipe PRs. A lot overlaps, but there are a few areas where mine goes deeper because they bit me in real PRs — sharing in case it's useful to fold in:

### 1. Upstream sourcing — pick up @seb-jean's point

Neither of our skills points to the **component source** (`apps/v4/styles/radix-nova/ui/<recipe>.tsx`), only to the examples. The component file is what carries the canonical classes / structure / `data-*` surface — without it, you only see how examples *use* the component, not the component itself. I'd add it as the first source to read.

Also, listing examples is non-trivial — I have a concrete recipe for it:

```bash
# Find the MDX page that lists every example slug
gh api repos/shadcn-ui/ui/git/trees/main?recursive=1 --jq '.tree[].path' | grep '<recipe>'
# Then grab each .tsx referenced in the MDX:
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/shadcn-ui/ui/refs/heads/main/apps/v4/examples/radix/<example>.tsx
```

### 2. Local visual testing — the dual-repo gotcha

The biggest pain when validating a recipe locally is that **`ux` and `ux.symfony.com` must be on matching branches**, otherwise the assetmap explodes:

> The asset "./vendor/symfony/ux-toolkit/kits/shadcn/<other>/assets/controllers/<other>_controller.js" cannot be found in any asset map paths.

Worth a section like:

```bash
cd ux             && git checkout feat/toolkit-shadcn-<recipe>
cd ux.symfony.com && git checkout docs/shadcn-<recipe>
symfony php bin/console tailwind:build
```

### 3. ux.symfony.com companion PR — what actually goes in it

The skill says "open a companion PR" but doesn't spell out what it contains. From experience:

- `templates/toolkit/docs/shadcn/<recipe>.md.twig` extending `_base_component.md.twig`
- One `{{ toolkit_code_example(...) }}` per example file shipped (otherwise they don't render — silent failure)
- If JS: register the Stimulus controller in `assets/toolkit-shadcn.js` + `importmap.php`
- Rebuild Tailwind: `symfony php bin/console tailwind:build`

### 4. Hover/focus components — don't go pure CSS

Worth flagging explicitly: for `hover-card`, `tooltip`, `dropdown-menu`, `menubar`, **don't try `group-hover` + `group-focus-within` + `tabindex=0`**. It looks elegant but breaks: clicking the trigger leaves the content open after mouseleave, and removing `group-focus-within` kills keyboard a11y. Always go straight to a Stimulus controller with `openDelay`/`closeDelay` values.

Minimal pattern:

```js
static values = {
    openDelay: { type: Number, default: 0 },
    closeDelay: { type: Number, default: 0 },
};
show() { /* clear timeouts, set data-state=open after openDelay */ }
hide() { /* clear timeouts, set data-state=closed after closeDelay */ }
```

### 5. Named groups for nested open-state

For components with a nested structure (`menubar` has Menu+Sub, `dropdown-menu` has Root+Sub), **`in-data-[state=open]:visible` matches any ancestor**, so opening the parent also opens every child at once. Use named groups instead:

```
.group/<recipe>-menu          (parent with data-controller)
.group-data-[state=open]/<recipe>-menu:visible  (parent's content)
.group/<recipe>-sub           (sub with its own data-controller)
.group-data-[state=open]/<recipe>-sub:visible   (sub's content)
```

### 6. Animation: grid-template-rows, never `hidden`

For expand/collapse (accordion, collapsible, content panels):

```twig
<div class="grid overflow-hidden transition-[grid-template-rows] duration-300 ease-out"
     style="grid-template-rows: {{ open ? '1fr' : '0fr' }};">
    <div class="min-h-0 min-w-0 overflow-hidden">{%- block content %}{% endblock -%}</div>
</div>
```

`hidden` (display:none) causes layout jumps — only `grid-template-rows: 0fr` + `overflow:hidden` gives a clean transition.

### 7. Snapshot gotchas

Two things reviewers consistently flag and that the skill doesn't cover:

- **Orphan snapshots after a rework.** When you rename or convert `<details>` to a Stimulus version, you often end up with stale `Demo.html__1.html` (no `.twig` suffix) sitting next to the new `Demo.html.twig__1.html`. They are never regenerated — `git rm` them.
- **Re-regenerate after rebase on `3.x`.** The snapshot formatter evolves upstream; running `UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=true vendor/bin/phpunit --filter "<recipe>"` once more after the final rebase is what avoids "diff in snapshots" CI failures.

### 8. Trailing newlines on every shipped file

The skill mentions snapshots/lint but not this: **every shipped file must end with a newline** — `.html.twig`, `.json`, `.js`, `.css`, `.md`. Maintainers add them by hand at merge if missing, so worth doing it upfront. One-liner:

```bash
for f in <files>; do tail -c1 "$f" | od -c | grep -q '\\n' || printf '\n' >> "$f"; done
```

---

Happy to open a follow-up PR pulling these into your skill if you're open to it — or if you'd rather keep the skill lean for now, totally fair, just leaving them here for visibility 😊

